{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/317163-tel-aran-rhiod-the-world-of-dreams-in-exalted-lunars-and-dreams-theme-idea","id":317163,"title":"Tel'aran'rhiod, the world of dreams in exalted. Lunars and dreams theme idea.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-20T02:37:02-08:00","id":317163,"title":"Tel'aran'rhiod, the world of dreams in exalted. Lunars and dreams theme idea.","content":"<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tel&#39;aran&#39;rhiod\" target=\"_blank\">In Robert Jordans wheel of time series there is a setting element called Tel'aran'rhiod, the world of dreams.</a> This world is a dream-reflection of the waking world. All things in the world of dreams are geographically dependent on the real world. things which are sedentary in the real world such as mountains, forests, buildings and furniture tend to stay put in the world of dreams while things that move or see use, such as utensils, correspondence, tent or wagon encampments or tracks tend to pop in and out of existence since their passing fails to imprints itself on the dreamworld. Normal people may enter the dreamworld while asleep and usually remember this as a very vivid dream. The dreams and nightmares created by normal humans that find their way into the world of dreams sometimes stay put, adding to the weirdness of the world. Tel'aran'rhiod is thus filled with echoes of things that exist and things people wish existed and things people fear. There are artifacts that allow people to enter Tel'aran'rhiod with a higher lever of control and awareness, allowing the user to exploit the opportunities of the world of dreams. There are however some that can enter Tel'aran'rhiod consciously and purposefully on their own - dreamwalkers.<br /> <br /> People who find themselves in Tel'aran'rhiod can control the world of dreams by controlling their subconscious. A skilled dreamwalker can change their appearance, create scenery, levitate, instantly travel to any location in the dreamworld and so forth. Injuries in the world of dreams affect to bodies of dreamers back in the real world, so breaking your leg in a landslide imagined in a nightmare by some random sleeping human is a very real danger, not to mention if you come across another dreamwalker who might conjure up anything nasty they can imagine at you.<br /> <br /> So what are the benefits of the world of dreams? Well, a dreamer can for example take a birds eye view of a battlefield to plan a strategy, visit their enemies headquarters in hopes of finding some evidence of their next move pop into existance briefly, communicate with other dreamwalker allies across the world and evaluate a population or an individuals hopes and fears by observing and drawing conclusions from dream constructs they come across.<br /> <br /> Now why am I talking about this on the exalted forum then? Because this would be a great setting element for No Moon lunars. It can be a way to implement the vision quest and the shamanistic spirit world. Lunars could have a charmbranch based on dreamworld manipulation. It's a quirky, fun and thematically appropriate angle for lunars to be useful. It can be used as alternative to the sidereal heavenly google charm, the sorcery infalliable messenger and a way for lunars to do investigation in a way that is definatley not silver solar. In the exalted setting you could also have sidereals roam around in there when normal astrology or real-world investigation fails them and letting the place be tainted by the nightmares of the Neverborn allows the Abyssals a thematic way in as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> What do you folks think?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/327-drecain","name":"Drecain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T04:50:46-08:00","id":317285,"title":"","content":"I've seen a similar idea that was based more upon The Dreamlands of the Cthulhu Mythos proposed as an alternative (and more palatable) reason why the powers that be want Sacheverell to remain asleep. The idea is very sorcerous but there's worse places for Lunar magic to go and overlap isn't always a bad thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T05:13:30-08:00","id":317304,"title":"","content":"Just a note, the Yozi and their kind are not barred from entering dreams, their oath only bars them from Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T05:37:39-08:00","id":317314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/317163-tel-aran-rhiod-the-world-of-dreams-in-exalted-lunars-and-dreams-theme-idea?p=317304#post317304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a note, the Yozi and their kind are not barred from entering dreams, their oath only bars them from Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>More importantly, while the Yozis are barred from entering Creation by their oaths, no restriction keeps them from the realms of dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T07:20:23-08:00","id":317353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/317163-tel-aran-rhiod-the-world-of-dreams-in-exalted-lunars-and-dreams-theme-idea?p=317314#post317314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More importantly, while the Yozis are barred from entering Creation by their oaths, no restriction keeps them from the realms of dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't you just say the same thing again? Is there some subtlety I'm missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T07:26:04-08:00","id":317355,"title":"","content":"This notion of a dream world bothers me a lot, and I think the reason for that is that I don't want there to be a non-physical space where some splats or specialized characters can go and get an overwhelming advantage over other characters.<br /> <br /> Currently, ever other &quot;Realm&quot; besides creation is a physical space where you physically have to go to physically do stuff. Mind and body are not separated, and the effects of damage are the same everywhere. If there is some space where that principle isn't true, then you have to put protective measures in place to stop mages and other professional planeswalkers from going there and killing everyone in their sleep.<br /> <br /> Other games that include otherworld-like spaces at all have such preventative mechanisms, you will note. In<i>Shadowrun </i>you can't attack anyone that isn't also Astral while you're on the Astral plane, or do much of anything besides scout. In <i>Changling</i> it is expensive to enter people's dreams on a whim, and you can't do anything in there except mess with their minds. In <i>Unknown Armies</i> you might wander into an otherspace while you sleep, but for all intents and purposes you are physically there, and how imaginative you are won't impact how strong you are or what other abilities you might have.<br /> <br /> A place like Tel'aran'rhiod is cool as a concept, but as a gameplay space it would be deeply problematic because some characters would be entirely unable to access it while others would be disproportionately powerful there. You might find you've got something like the Decker problem in <i>Shadowrun</i>, in which characters who can effectively use the Matrix a) can basically leave the whole party behind while they go off to play in their special world that only they can really see or interact with and b) can utterly screw up anyone who is dependent on Matrix-using technology but is not personally a Decker, which includes most people who aren't magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T08:05:02-08:00","id":317377,"title":"","content":"While I do understand semicasual's point, I feel as if an Exalted take on the dreamworld would probably involve preventative mechanisms as well- something uniquely exalted, like &quot;you are physically a part of the sleeping world, and while other people can be present mentally in their sleep, you can only hurt other people who are physically present&quot;. Or something, I'm not a dev.<br /> <br /> I do feel it raises another problem when you start tying it into Lunars, though, because it's really just adding to the thematic incoherency that's dogged the splat through the last two editions. Lunars are already animalistic-shapeshifter-barbarians-who-defend-against-the-wyld-and-serve-luna-but-also-gaia-kind-of-because-of-the-animal-thing-and-are-stewards-of-creation-and-social-engineers*. Do we really to further dilute that with -and-have-special-dream-magic?<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I think there's something worth looking at here. We've already talked about how the yozis are free to enter the dreaming realm, and I could see the dead and the wyld being able to access it too, maybe. It'd certainly provide an interesting battleground. And kind of explain why the Lunars have been sitting on their asses since the usurpation. And it fits with Luna a bit better then the animal stuff does currently...<br /> <br /> ...and somehow I'm talking myself around to this idea. Hmm. This, I think I shall ponder.<br /> <br /> *Or at least that's what they've been in the past. We'll see what the devs do with them this time around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/768-djehuty3","name":"djehuty3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T08:08:58-08:00","id":317379,"title":"","content":"Sounds like the Sea of Mind, which the Ebon Dragon has an embassy in. Though that isn't quite as accessible to everyone.<br /> <br /> Infernal Monster expansions also had a few dream fight charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T09:57:39-08:00","id":317491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaaace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/317163-tel-aran-rhiod-the-world-of-dreams-in-exalted-lunars-and-dreams-theme-idea?p=317353#post317353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't you just say the same thing again? Is there some subtlety I'm missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>He said &quot;Yozi,&quot; as in just one imprisoned Primordial. I said &quot;Yozi<i>s</i>,&quot; indicating that more than just the one can do it. If just Ebby could do it, that'd be one thing, but Oramus has been known to send his souls across the gulfs as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T10:07:42-08:00","id":317525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/317163-tel-aran-rhiod-the-world-of-dreams-in-exalted-lunars-and-dreams-theme-idea?p=317491#post317491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He said &quot;Yozi,&quot; as in just one imprisoned Primordial. I said &quot;Yozi<i>s</i>,&quot; indicating that more than just the one can do it. If just Ebby could do it, that'd be one thing, but Oramus has been known to send his souls across the gulfs as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't this getting a little pedantic? I mean its a game, a lot of people make the mistake, and it is clear from context that it is meant to be plural. It isn't like the secret order of grammar-ninjas that predates the Primordials will use their fourth wall breaking SMA to slap you if you type it wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T10:35:22-08:00","id":317542,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/171957-the-dreaming\">I had a similar idea once! </a> If there's anything you like there, take it and run with it...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T10:49:46-08:00","id":317554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/317163-tel-aran-rhiod-the-world-of-dreams-in-exalted-lunars-and-dreams-theme-idea?p=317525#post317525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't this getting a little pedantic? I mean its a game, a lot of people make the mistake, and it is clear from context that it is meant to be plural. It isn't like the secret order of grammar-ninjas that predates the Primordials will use their fourth wall breaking SMA to slap you if you type it wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Essentially this. Also I always refer the plural of Yozi as Yozi, for they are grand, they are one and multiple, damn your &quot;Yozis&quot;.You don't called the Neverborns now do you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T11:04:46-08:00","id":317577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/317163-tel-aran-rhiod-the-world-of-dreams-in-exalted-lunars-and-dreams-theme-idea?p=317355#post317355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This notion of a dream world bothers me a lot, and I think the reason for that is that I don't want there to be a non-physical space where some splats or specialized characters can go and get an overwhelming advantage over other characters.<br /> <br /> Currently, ever other &quot;Realm&quot; besides creation is a physical space where you physically have to go to physically do stuff. Mind and body are not separated, and the effects of damage are the same everywhere. If there is some space where that principle isn't true, then you have to put protective measures in place to stop mages and other professional planeswalkers from going there and killing everyone in their sleep.<br /> <br /> Other games that include otherworld-like spaces at all have such preventative mechanisms, you will note. In<i>Shadowrun </i>you can't attack anyone that isn't also Astral while you're on the Astral plane, or do much of anything besides scout. In <i>Changling</i> it is expensive to enter people's dreams on a whim, and you can't do anything in there except mess with their minds. In <i>Unknown Armies</i> you might wander into an otherspace while you sleep, but for all intents and purposes you are physically there, and how imaginative you are won't impact how strong you are or what other abilities you might have.<br /> <br /> A place like Tel'aran'rhiod is cool as a concept, but as a gameplay space it would be deeply problematic because some characters would be entirely unable to access it while others would be disproportionately powerful there. You might find you've got something like the Decker problem in <i>Shadowrun</i>, in which characters who can effectively use the Matrix a) can basically leave the whole party behind while they go off to play in their special world that only they can really see or interact with and b) can utterly screw up anyone who is dependent on Matrix-using technology but is not personally a Decker, which includes most people who aren't magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>All valid concerns. <br /> <br /> First off - In the WoT books, the world of dreams is not just for dreamwalkers since there are artifacts that allow anyone who sleeps with them touching their skin to enter regardless if they can use magic or not.<br /> <br /> Another thing is that Tel'aran'rhiod is void of people by default. Normal humans might find themselves there as they sleep, but they usually pop right out again since they dont have the skill to manipulate their subconcious. So it's like how it worked in shadowrun (I guess, haven't played it)<br /> <br /> It is also quite easy to hide what you're doing from a dreamwalker - just dont leave physical evidence and it wont show up in the world of dreams. The thing in the books is the just the protagonists and one of the antagonist factions know about it..<br /> <br /> In exalted I could totally see the world being a hunting ground for demons as well as living neverborn nightmares. I personally would leave the fair folk barred from the world of dreams since I think they'd.. Y'know.. Eat it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":327,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/327-drecain","user":"Drecain","date":". 11-20-2014, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/327-drecain","name":"Drecain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T11:22:17-08:00","id":317588,"title":"","content":"Ooh. Another problem I can see with the idea is the craft problem. One character has the charms/artifact to go spirit questing to the world of dreams and the rest of the party has to guard his/her sleeping body? Mhhh :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/327-drecain","name":"Drecain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T11:28:42-08:00","id":317590,"title":"","content":"In the Wheel of Time series, there was an instance were someone who was not a dreamwalker was pulled into Tel'aran'rhiod by a dreamwalker. After an initial period of confusion, he caught on to the metaphysics pretty quick, though he was still far outclassed by the standards of dreamwalkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3976-silent-witness","name":"Silent Witness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3976_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T15:32:24-08:00","id":317726,"title":"","content":"Normally I like dreamscapes, but...<br /> <br /> Well, it doesn't mesh with the parts of how dreams work in Creation that I like. Dreamstones, dream flies, the gods in Yu-Shan whose job is is to craft dreams, Raksha's love of eating human dreamstuff (which they like because human passions are REAL, and if it's because human passions are a link to this dreamy otherworld it makes Creation's solidity seem less the source of it-Raksha shouldn't be hungering for something that's just another Wyld). The dreams of the Neverborn and the Yozi are already worlds you can travel in anyway.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of effects that let you communicate with your friends or attack your enemies through their dreams, or even charms that let you travel through dreams and arrive somewhere else while awake...but I don't think we need a whole additional realm in the cosmology for that to work, and I don't like the idea of dreams being this place where special people are matrix-fighting with each other that &quot;real&quot; sleepers can't get into. If you're traveling in dreams, it oughta be dangerous for you BECAUSE the real sleepers aren't in danger and have total control over the place on an unconscious level. Traveling in someone else's mindscape oughta be like traveling inside Malfeas-the world is alive and aware and not your own.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T15:48:38-08:00","id":317737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/317163-tel-aran-rhiod-the-world-of-dreams-in-exalted-lunars-and-dreams-theme-idea?p=317554#post317554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Essentially this. Also I always refer the plural of Yozi as Yozi, for they are grand, they are one and multiple, damn your &amp;quot;Yozis&amp;quot;.You don't called the Neverborns now do you?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's idiotic; Yozis has precedent by dint of being written that way by Lord Dunsany. Just like Neverborn has precedent by dint of being written that way in <i>Wraith: the Oblivion</i>. <br /> <br /> I don't ask my sister to get two &quot;loaves of breads,&quot; I don't ask a friend if he's read &quot;all the book&quot; by George R. R. Martin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T18:04:15-08:00","id":317829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/317163-tel-aran-rhiod-the-world-of-dreams-in-exalted-lunars-and-dreams-theme-idea?p=317737#post317737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's idiotic; Yozis has precedent by dint of being written that way by Lord Dunsany. Just like Neverborn has precedent by dint of being written that way in <i>Wraith: the Oblivion</i>.<br /> <br /> I don't ask my sister to get two &quot;loaves of breads&quot;...</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZjtA30DQdDU\" target=\"_blank\">Maybe <i>you</i> don't...</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 11-20-2014, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T18:55:56-08:00","id":317859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/317163-tel-aran-rhiod-the-world-of-dreams-in-exalted-lunars-and-dreams-theme-idea?p=317737#post317737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's idiotic; Yozis has precedent by dint of being written that way by Lord Dunsany. Just like Neverborn has precedent by dint of being written that way in <i>Wraith: the Oblivion</i>.<br /> <br /> I don't ask my sister to get two &quot;loaves of breads,&quot; I don't ask a friend if he's read &quot;all the book&quot; by George R. R. Martin.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I didn't know inspiration mean't you had to take the idea entirely wholesale. Damn the &quot;Yozis&quot; I do it mostly as a literary quirk strictly for the Primordial. All other plurals end in s, except in the context of the Primordial. They are the Yozi, or the Neverborn. Why? Because they are the Primordial, that's why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T19:43:18-08:00","id":317874,"title":"","content":"You might go buy &quot;two fish&quot;, or drink &quot;three beer&quot;. Maybe eat a couple of grilled octopi while observing a herd of deer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T20:18:18-08:00","id":317889,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">It's probably a good idea not to come up with your own linguistic conventions and then expect others to understand what you mean, especially when going against already established nomenclature. I think people getting upset with intentional misuse is understandable, let's not be jerks in expressing that frustration, ok?</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br 